-  - Chose: configs stored as content-addressed blobs (hash) with signed manifests; Postgres stores rollout state (“cohort → version”).
-  - Rejected: mutable key-value updates as “the config.”
-  - Why: rollback becomes an O(1) pointer change; audit is trivial; agents can safely cache and verify.
